  "description_text": "Discover a unique opportunity at 753 Capp Street, nestled in the heart of San Francisco's vibrant Mission District. This beautifully updated garden-level residence is part of a grand three-unit Victorian triplex, showcasing stunning historic Stick/Eastlake architectural charm on the exterior with modern updates and systems throughout. Offering 5 bedrooms and 4 bathrooms, this spacious home features a contemporary kitchen with stainless steel appliances and thoughtfully updated interiors. Tucked away at the rear of the building, the unit provides a peaceful and quiet retreat from the city, with direct garden access from two rear bedrooms. Additional conveniences include shared laundry facilities, with ample space within the unit to install your own stacked washer and dryer. Enjoy the vibrant Mission District lifestyle with convenient access to iconic Dolores Park, Valencia Street's popular dining and shopping destinations, neighborhood playgrounds, and the renowned murals of Balmy and Clarion Alleys. Nearby BART, Muni, and major commuter routes provide additional convenience. A wonderful opportunity to own a spacious, character-filled home in one of San Francisco's most vibrant neighborhoods and close to Mission Dolores Park! The property is part of a three-unit building, 751 - top unit; 753 - middle unit; 753A - lower unit (subject). Additional units 751 and 753 available for purchase separately or together. Can be delivered vacant.",
